<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;opinion&nbsp;post</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;click&nbsp;HERE&nbsp;to&nbsp;close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This one’s pretty alright. It’s evident that they treat each individual section as a different individual, which is pretty interesting.</p>
<p>-1 is treated with respect because it gives respect (and is most obviously the original person, who wasn’t exactly a murderer and was given professional respect by researchers), -3 has no real ability to self-control and the Doctor is stricter with hierarchy, -2 was spoken with politely and straightforward because it communicates so rarely.</p>
<p>Professional but succinct, the doctor stays only as long as necessary with each interview.</p>
<p>Not a big fan of the Vinz Clortho cameo but I’m reasonably certain that most Sarkic type SCPs are intentionally OTT in that regard.</p>
